// unconstrained token, or open a span with OpenConstrainedSpan, which sets the
// constrained prefix to []. In the recovery branch, rollback returns a
// parser-valid repaired prefix; trimming generated to the same length preserves
// validity. In the constrained append branches, AdaptiveConstrainedStep and
// GroupBoostedConstrainedStep guarantee the sampled token is EOS or valid next;
// on non-EOS, AppendConstrainedToken preserves parser-validity. In the close
// branch, insideConstrainedOut becomes false, so the implication is vacuous.
//
// suffix: Outside constrained mode the invariant is vacuous. Opening a span
// appends only the delimiter and resets currentConstrainedOut to [], so the
// suffix of length 0 matches. In recovery, repaired is a prefix of the old
// constrained content, and generated is trimmed by exactly the removed suffix
// length, so the new generated suffix equals repaired. In constrained append
// branches, AppendConstrainedToken appends the same token to generated and the
// constrained prefix, preserving suffix equality. Closing makes inside false,
// so the implication is vacuous.
