// AdaptiveConstrainedStep, or GroupBoostedConstrainedStep each perform one
// cost-bumping helper action. The pure recovery branch uses only rollback and
// trimming, so it explicitly does steps := steps + 1. Therefore cost := steps
// satisfies cost <= maxSteps.
//
// progress: UnconstrainedStep appends one token and the branch increments steps
// by 1. OpenConstrainedSpan appends one token and increments steps by 1.
// CloseConstrainedSpan appends at most one token and increments steps by 1.
// Adaptive/group-boosted constrained branches append one token via
